warnings in scanner:\n```\ninline int nextInt() {\n    char c = getChar();\n    while(c <= ' ' && c) c=getChar();\n    int sign=1;\n    if(c=='-'){sign=-1;c=getChar();}\n    long long x=0;\n    for(; c>='0'&&c<='9'; c=getChar()) x = x*10 + (c-'0');\n    return (int)(sign*x);\n}\n```\nIf EOF, returns 0 but input valid.\n\nNeed maybe use `fread` from stdin. Include `<unistd.h>`? no.\n\nLet's think about performance: Reading matrix into flat vector row-major; vertical update accesses a[inRow*n+j] and a[outRow*n+j], contiguous over j for fixed rows, good SIMD. Initialization column access strided but only once per thread block (4 times). Horizontal pref sequential O(n) per row; total O(N^2/threads + threads*S*N). For large S, initialization overhead could be significant: 4 * S * N ~ if S=4000,N=8000 =>128M operations, okay. Main work horizontal prefix and update: each thread processes ~totalRows/nt rows; for each row pref O(n) plus update O(n), total ~2*N^2 =128M ops across threads? Actually 4 threads * (N^2/4)*2 =128M, good.\n\nCould further optimize by using column prefix sums to initialize v in O(n) per thread instead of O(S*n). But memory tradeoff. Maybe use a shared `vector<long long> colPrefix` only if n small? Not needed.\n\nNeed ensure all valid sizes correct: For each top row r from base to base+len-1, vertical window sums are exactly sum rows r..r+s-1. Initialization for base; update subtract outRow and add inRow where inRow = previous r + s = current r + s -1? Let's verify:\nAt process_row(r), v[j] should equal sum_{k=r}^{r+s-1} a[k*n+j].\nInitial at r=base correct.\nTransition from r to r+1: subtract row r, add row r+s. In code outRow = base+idx-1 (previous r), inRow = outRow + s = previous r + s = current r + s -? Wait if previous r = p, new r=p+1; window rows [p+1, p+s]. Remove row p, add row p+s. So inRow = p+s = (new r)+s-1. Code `inRow = outRow + s` correct.\nThen process_row(base+idx) uses updated v.\n\nHorizontal max over windows starting j=0..n-s: pref[j+s]-pref[j] where pref[i]=sum_{t< i} v[t]. Correct.\n\nOutput best as long long; final guaranteed int32 but okay.\n\nNeed maybe use `int` for matrix values. Scanner returns int.\n\nPotential issue with OpenMP reduction and manual chunking: If nt > totalRows, some threads len=0 skip. Good.\n```\nif (len == 0) { /* nothing */ } else { ... }\n```\n\nCould avoid lambda overhead by inline code or define local function? Lambda may be inlined at -O3.\n\nNeed include `omp.h`; if OpenMP disabled, omp_get_num_threads returns 1 and pragmas ignored. But build likely with -fopenmp. If not, still compiles because omp.h available? Maybe not. Previous experiments used OpenMP so okay.\n\nLet's craft final source code carefully.\n\nPotential warning: `#pragma omp simd reduction(max:mxSum)` inside parallel region where mxSum is shared reduction variable; GCC may warn \"user defined reduction not found\"? No, max built-in supported for integer types in C++? OpenMP spec supports max/min reductions for integer and floating point. Should be fine.\n\nPotential warning: `pref[i+1] = pref[i] + v[i];` no issue.\n\nNeed maybe use `std::vector<long long> v(n);` inside parallel region; allocation per thread okay.\n\nLet's write code:\n\n```\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n#include <climits>\n#include <omp.h>\n\nclass FastScanner {\n    static const int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\n    int idx, size;\n    char buf[BUFSIZE];\npublic:\n    FastScanner() : idx(0), size(0) {}\n    inline int nextInt() {\n        char c;\n        do { c = getChar(); } while (c <= ' ' && c);\n        int sign = 1;\n        if (c == '-') { sign = -1; c = getChar(); }\n        long long x = 0;\n        for (; c >= '0' && c <= '9'; c = getChar()) {\n            x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n        }\n        return static_cast<int>(sign * x);\n    }\nprivate:\n    inline char getChar() {\n        if (idx >= size) {\n            size = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n            idx = 0;\n            if (size == 0) return '\\0';\n        }\n        return buf[idx++];\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastScanner fs;\n    int n = fs.nextInt();\n    int s = fs.nextInt();\n\n    std::vector<int> a(static_cast<size_t>(n) * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        int* row = &a[static_cast<size_t>(i) * n];\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            row[j] = fs.nextInt();\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long mxSum = -(1LL << 62);\n    const int totalRows = n - s + 1;\n\n#pragma omp parallel reduction(max:mxSum)\n    {\n        const int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\n        const int nt = omp_get_num_threads();\n\n        std::vector<long long> v(n);\n        std::vector<long long> pref(n + 1);\n\n        // contiguous block of starting rows for this thread\n        int base = (totalRows / nt) * tid + (tid < totalRows % nt ? tid : totalRows % nt);\n        int len = totalRows / nt + (tid < totalRows % nt ? 1 : 0);\n\n        if (len > 0) {\n            // vertical sums for the first row assigned to this thread\n            const int* baseRow = &a[static_cast<size_t>(base) * n];\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n                long long t = 0;\n                for (int k = 0; k < s; ++k) {\n                    t += a[static_cast<size_t>(base + k) * n + j];\n                }\n                v[j] = t;\n            }\n\n            // process first row\n            pref[0] = 0;\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) pref[i + 1] = pref[i] + v[i];\n#pragma omp simd reduction(max:mxSum)\n            for (int j = 0; j <= n - s; ++j) {\n                long long w = pref[j + s] - pref[j];\n                if (w > mxSum) mxSum = w;\n            }\n\n            // slide vertically through the remaining rows in this block\n            for (int idx = 1; idx < len; ++idx) {\n                const int outRow = base + idx - 1;\n                const int inRow = outRow + s;\n                const long long*? no, use int pointers.\n                const int* outPtr = &a[static_cast<size_t>(outRow) * n];\n                const int* inPtr = &a[static_cast<size_t>(inRow) * n];\n#pragma omp simd\n                for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n                    v[j] += static_cast<long long>(inPtr[j]) - outPtr[j];\n                }\n\n                pref[0] = 0;\n                for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) pref[i + 1] = pref[i] + v[i];\n#pragma omp simd reduction(max:mxSum)\n                for (int j = 0; j <= n - s; ++j) {\n                    long long w = pref[j + s] - pref[j];\n                    if (w > mxSum) mxSum = w;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\nNeed check `base` formula for contiguous blocks:\nStandard: base = tid * chunk_size where chunk_size = totalRows/nt, plus remainder distributed to first rem threads. Formula:\n```\nint q = totalRows / nt;\nint r = totalRows % nt;\nint begin = tid < r ? tid*(q+1) : r*(q+1)+(tid-r)*q;\nint len = q + (tid<r);\n```\nOur formula `(totalRows/nt)*tid + (tid < rem ? tid : rem)` is wrong. Example total=10, nt=4: q=2,r=2; t0 base=0*2+0=0,len3; t1 base=1*2+1=3,len3; t2 base=2*2+2? tid<r false => +rem=2 ->6,len2; t3 base=3*2+2=8,len2. Blocks: [0,2],[3,5],[6,7],[8,9] correct. Example total=10, nt=3 q=3,r=1: t0 base=0+0=0 len4; t1 base=3+1? tid<r false => +rem=1 ->4 len3; t2 base=6+1=7 len3 => blocks [0..3],[4..6],[7..9] correct. Example total=5, nt=8 q=0,r=5: t0 base=0*0+0=0 len1; t1 base=0*1? formula (total/nt)*tid =0 + tid<r ? tid : rem => for t1 true ->1 len1; ... t4 base=0+4=4 len1; t5 false ->5 but totalRows 5, len0. Good. So formula works: `base = q*tid + (tid < r ? tid : r);` where q=total/nt, r=total%nt. Our code uses `(totalRows / nt) * tid + (tid < rem ? tid : rem)` yes correct.\n\nNeed ensure `len > 0`, and base+idx-1 within totalRows-1; for last thread len maybe q or q+1; okay.\n\nPotential issue: If n=0? constraints n>0. s<n so totalRows>=1.\n\nPotential warning: unused variable `baseRow` in initializatio